# Tower Clash — App Store listing / review request (MM-12, docs/MOBILE.md §3.2).
#
# Pushing a change of this file to the branch claude/tower-war-game-plan-weqwpb starts
# .github/workflows/tower-clash-ios-store.yml once (fastlane deliver with the App Store Connect
# API key). Pushes to any other branch start nothing. Without the four Apple secrets the run stops
# in its first step, "Check required secrets". Nothing is ever released to the public by this
# file: the version is set to "Manually release this version" and waits for the stakeholder's
# "Release This Version" click after approval.
#
# Keys (one key=value per line; lines starting with # are ignored; unknown keys are an error):
#   action     metadata — upload texts (fastlane/metadata), screenshots, age rating, categories,
#                         price Free + the four soft-launch countries (only if not set yet) and the
#                         TestFlight group "Team"; never submits
#              submit   — the same, then selects build <build> of the package.json version,
#                         answers export compliance (no non-exempt encryption) and content rights
#                         (no third-party content) and submits the version for App Review; needs
#                         the four ASC_REVIEW_* secrets and the contact e-mail on the privacy page
#   build      the build number to submit, e.g. 8 (required for submit; ignored by metadata)
#   iphone65   yes = also upload the 6.5" set (store/screenshots/apple-6.5/en); default no, the
#              6.9" set (apple-6.7/en, 1290x2796) is the only one App Store Connect requires
#   note       free text for the log, at most 200 characters
#   requested  UTC time of the request, e.g. 2026-10-09T15:30:00Z — change it every time
action=metadata
build=
iphone65=no
note=MM-12 first request: expected to stop at the secrets check until the stakeholder adds the Apple secrets
requested=2026-10-09T16:00:00Z
